/-!
# The graph-field alternative in the inner-action family argument

The source branch has L/O₂(L) ≅ PSL₃(4) with the specified graph-field
action of r. `Geometry` constructs E = ⟨r,z⟩, the Sylow-normalizer choice,
and a compatible conjugator. `Endgame` proves the Frattini placement and
product contradiction for a placed centerless complement, and the
quasithin obstruction to an independent centralizing three-element.

`ModelData` publishes the remaining intrinsic contracts on actual subgroups
and relative quotients. Their witnesses, the paired transvections and
Frattini argument in the cover case, the normal residual intersection,
the GL₂(3) contradiction, and the centerless quotient placement are still
required. Thus this module does not yet assert the graph-field exclusion
or source 16.4.9(2). Final assembly remains here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of 16.4.9(2), printed pp.1191–1192.
-/
